Separate behaviour from role selection. A compact pseudocode shape is:
interface User { authenticate(username, password); createAccount(username, password, extraInfo); }
class Customer implements User { customer-specific methods }
class Manager implements User { manager-specific methods }
class UserFactory { create(role) → Customer or Manager; reject unsupported roles }
UserController: user = factory.create(role); user.authenticate(...) or user.createAccount(...).
The controller now depends on User rather than hardcoded role branches; add a role by implementing User and updating the factory’s creation mapping.
